Considering the good response from my last post ("A few hopefully good
suggestions") I'm starting this thread to discuss and raise
suggestions the next NH versions. Fell free to add your own
 
- Kick small monsters to throw them away (as in the last message)
The kick has never been really useful in combat, I suggest that
kicking a small monster would have the same result as kicking an light
object (throwing them away), I think this is a great way to avoid
(cock/chick)atrices when you have boots as well as escape/avoid
annoying monsters when needed by keeping distance.
 
- Takedown/fall down
This might also be interesting, by kick, by attacking or throwing
something heavy (like a corpse), the opponent may loose his balance
fall to the ground, becoming exposed to your attack for one or two
turns. This would add some balance (or call it even more advantage) to
big creatures vs smaller creatures, for example: A troll hitting a
rogue with a war hammer taking the rogue down. *or* A rogue taking a
troll down after attacking him from behind. Of course, this would only
work on biped creatures.
 
- Caring a notepad
I believe this may have already been suggested, but in any case, a
notepad (starting with it or finding it) would be great for you to
make your own notes during the game and reading them anytime, also,
you could be able to view it after dying.
 
- Improved #chat with certain people for certain actions
An altar priest may charge (a considerably high tax) you to
uncurse/bless one of your items. Shopkeepers charge you to identify
items limited to their specialty (if it's a armor dealership, he will
only identify armors).
 
- Looking at the pictures have taken with your expensive camera (after
all, it's expensive)
I know that there is a patch for it, but since I didn't seen it and I
really thing it should be added to NetHack, here's the way I think it
should work: You take your pictures, after you quit/die/ascend you
will have the option to see your pictures. The way you see them would
be similar to your area of view of the direction of the picture when
you took it. Like this (notice the field of view):
      ---
    .....|
  .......|
@.....D
  .......|
    .....|
      ---
(Of course, you (@) would not appear)
 
I'm waiting for your comments!

